1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:05,000
What happens when a new chat begins, but
your project is only halfway finished? The

2
00:00:05,009 --> 00:00:07,658
useful details should
have somewhere to wait.

3
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:13,140
A product of Wayne Tech Lab, dot System
X starts with a familiar idea: a folder.

4
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:16,120
[soft instrumental music]

5
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:20,670
A blank sheet becomes
a folder on your desk.

6
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:25,600
It holds the goal, the plan, what
happened, and what comes next. Follow

7
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:30,400
one small community garden website from
its first request to a reviewed result.

8
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:38,440
The template supplies labeled
records and optional tools.

9
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:42,490
Your project records begin blank,
ready for your information.

10
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:45,664
An empty directory alone
has no special behavior.

11
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,378
Its value comes from the
structure and how you use it.

12
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:57,720
Headless means the format needs no
particular graphical control app or

13
00:00:57,740 --> 00:01:01,380
dedicated running server. You
can read the files directly.

14
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:04,392
Your chosen assistant supplies the model,

15
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:07,480
and its authorized tools
perform the actual work.

16
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:15,980
Python three point nine or newer
runs the included command tools

17
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,700
using its standard library. Reading
documents needs no Python process.

18
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:25,677
Git, provider commands, and cloud
connectors are separate when selected.

19
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:28,705
Keep the dot and uppercase
spelling shown here.

20
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:36,260
First, give the project
its context. For our garden

21
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:40,220
website, that means the audience,
meeting location, approved

22
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:44,400
content, and important limits.
Keep agreed facts and useful

23
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:47,832
references here, instead of
collecting every conversation.

24
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:56,560
Next comes the Master Plan.
Visitors should find garden hours,

25
00:01:56,740 --> 00:02:00,220
read joining instructions,
and follow working navigation.

26
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:04,720
Milestones describe meaningful
checkpoints. Add detail when

27
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:08,858
it helps the next decision, rather
than filling every possible branch.

28
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:17,520
The task ledger records ownership,
progress, dependencies, and evidence.

29
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:22,040
To do, working, review, and done
pages are views of that ledger.

30
00:02:22,580 --> 00:02:25,300
Memory retains reviewed
facts and a next step,

31
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:27,851
helping another session find its bearings.

32
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:35,540
Follow one card: verify the
garden information page.

33
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:40,020
Agent Zero coordinates its scope,
owner, and acceptance checks.

34
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:43,880
The task keeps its identity
as it moves. Generating a

35
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:47,196
page and meeting the agreed
result are different things.

36
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:54,100
A person or authorized assistant uses

37
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:57,400
actual tools to edit the
website and run its check.

38
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:01,400
Agent X records meaningful
events, times, and evidence.

39
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:05,460
It also tracks due items, but
does not run scheduled jobs.

40
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:13,904
Our synthetic example intentionally
leaves the opening hours out.

41
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:16,700
The check fails and identifies that gap.

42
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:20,040
We correct the page, then
run the same check again.

43
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:24,090
Retained receipts show the failed
input and corrected result.

44
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:32,920
Acceptance still needs review.
Agent Z scores supplied answers

45
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:36,293
against the same hundred
questions for its chosen policy.

46
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:40,600
Unknowns stay visible. Its
score advises the decision;

47
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:44,880
Agent Zero or the user accepts
against the original criteria.

48
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:53,404
A useful prompt gives the assistant
a destination and a boundary.

49
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:57,500
Start with: use this project's
existing dot System X.

50
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:02,200
Read the current context, Master
Plan, task ledger, and next step.

51
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:05,230
Help me finish the
community garden website.

52
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:13,700
Then add: identify finished work,
plan the next bounded tasks,

53
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:17,740
use available authorized tools,
and save verified results.

54
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,880
Ask when a decision or access is missing.

55
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:24,398
A prompt does not install
tools or grant permissions.

56
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:32,380
Some work can happen together.
One worker checks wording

57
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:36,880
while another checks navigation, with
clear assignments and write areas.

58
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:39,800
Agent Zero tracks dependencies and

59
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:43,173
brings their results back for
integration and acceptance.

60
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:51,400
The app starts its supported
subagents. Dot System X keeps

61
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:55,080
assignments, selected memory,
results, and checkpoints.

62
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:58,440
A role entry is a coordination record, not

63
00:04:58,460 --> 00:05:01,225
proof that another model
or process is running.

64
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:11,400
Agent Y uses one selected, installed
command line provider for a bounded task.

65
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:16,440
An owned worktree and optional draft
pull request keep its work reviewable.

66
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:19,740
Acceptance, merging, and
cleanup stay separate;

67
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:22,079
this lane never merges code itself.

68
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:30,200
The project ledger, assistant
task list, and optional bot

69
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:33,720
list can describe related work
with different item counts.

70
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:38,420
Root explicitly links their items
to stable project task identities.

71
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:41,173
Agreement does not mean identical lists.

72
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:50,240
An observation saves what was reported,
when, its revision, and evidence.

73
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:54,799
The Root comparison reads those
snapshots and highlights differences.

74
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:59,600
It does not contact live providers or
keep every list continuously synchronized.

75
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:07,740
Agent Zero checks affected
state, makes a justified

76
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:10,460
authorized correction, and reads it back.

77
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:14,740
A worker saying completed can
still mean the task needs review.

78
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:18,832
Missing access or stale
information remains a visible gap.

79
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:27,480
Useful detail needs a home.
Agent Alpha selects references

80
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:32,240
from the optional Autobot panel:
a cabinet of ten labeled drawers.

81
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:37,840
For this page, we might open Design and
Brand, leaving unrelated material closed.

82
00:06:42,580 --> 00:06:46,560
The drawers cover design,
purpose and voice, memory, rules,

83
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:50,520
research, brand, media, design
tokens, data, and archives.

84
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:54,138
They are reference functions,
not ten running models.

85
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:58,340
Alpha is separate. Matching
unchanged requests can reuse

86
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:01,713
retained results instead of
starting the same work again.

87
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:09,400
Root holds internal rules,
planning links, and tool

88
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:13,060
cards describing bounded
actions and expected evidence.

89
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:16,209
They connect to the
existing plan and ledger.

90
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:21,480
They do not override current instructions,
install tools, or execute automatically.

91
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:30,960
Data folders hold working files,
imports, research, assets, exports,

92
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:35,440
cache, and archives. Supplied Git
rules ignore payloads by default.

93
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,565
That is not encryption
or cloud sharing policy.

94
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:41,293
A file pointer is not upload permission.

95
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:50,600
One outer installation serves named
projects. Our website and separate

96
00:07:50,620 --> 00:07:54,880
garden research project each have
their own dot System X P records:

97
00:07:55,380 --> 00:07:58,040
context, plan, tasks, and memory.

98
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:02,404
They share outer tools while keeping
project information separate.

99
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:10,560
Select the project for every
handoff. A repository, local

100
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:14,220
drive, or authorized cloud
location can carry records.

101
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:18,390
A web address alone creates no
connection or synchronization.

102
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:22,219
Writers need agreed ownership
and fresh saved state.

103
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:30,420
Before stopping, retain
results, evidence, open

104
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:34,580
questions, and the exact next
action. Another session reads

105
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:37,718
the relevant records and
checks changing facts again.

106
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:42,573
Continuity comes from that handoff,
not automatic memory inside the model.

107
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:51,920
Selected context can reduce repeated
explanations and avoidable rework.

108
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:57,460
Maintaining records also costs time and
tokens, so measure the complete workflow.

109
00:08:57,900 --> 00:09:01,460
Keep the useful cards close
and unrelated history closed.

110
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:04,177
Clear information helps the next turn.

111
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:12,180
Choose a reviewed version.
Updates are manual by default;

112
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:15,489
optional startup notices
report availability.

113
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:19,703
Managed updates preserve adopted
records and add selected defaults.

114
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:24,760
Keep backups and removal receipts.
This is experimental alpha software.

115
00:09:24,780 --> 00:09:29,360
Local checks, publication, and
live verification remain separate.

116
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:38,660
Start with one project, one useful
plan, and one verifiable task.

117
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:42,219
The four maps now describe
a path you have followed.

118
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:45,439
Visit the repository and
Start Here guide on screen.

119
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:48,877
Keep your evidence reviewable
and your next step clear.

120
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:54,900
